WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.850
Hey David, can you address the issue that
came up on Joe Rogan's show when you were

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:10.461
interviewed, where Joe Equated with Steven
Crowder did to Carlos Mazda to what Sam Cedar

00:00:10.461 --> 00:00:12.060
does to Dave Rubin?

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:16.520
Listen, I actually, in watching that back,
I think that people may have misunderstood.

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:22.910
I didn't interpret what Joe Rogan was doing
as actually equating the homophobic harassment

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:28.190
by Steven Crowder of Carlos Mazda to Sam Cedar
making videos about Dave Ruben.

00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:32.369
But I do think that I missed an opportunity
to much more clearly sort of explore, explain

00:00:32.369 --> 00:00:33.369
my position.

00:00:33.369 --> 00:00:38.920
And the best way I can say it is when Sam
Cedar Critiques Dave Ruben, he's criticizing

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:42.640
Dave Rubin for what he says, not for who he
is.

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:47.489
Dave Rubin's identity plays no role in Sam
cedars critiques of Dave Rubin.

00:00:47.489 --> 00:00:49.449
Dave Rubin happens to be Jewish.

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:51.260
Dave Rubin happens to be gay.

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:53.429
Dave Rubin happens to be male.

00:00:53.429 --> 00:00:59.969
None of those characteristics have ever played
a role in Sam's criticisms of Dave Ruben when

00:00:59.969 --> 00:01:07.040
Steven Crowder is including phrases like lispy
be Mexican queer when he is talking about

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:08.070
Carlos Mazda.

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:14.920
Even if you want to argue that the critique
was about Antifa as as uh, came up during

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:20.670
my Joe Rogan appearance, you are getting into
critiques that are critiques of who Carlos

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:22.480
Mazda is as a person.

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:23.550
And what, where is that coming?

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:24.550
I don't know what that is.

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:25.880
That is a very strange noise.

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:26.880
Apologies for that.

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:29.950
Uh, hopefully people didn't hear a very strange
ringing noise there.

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:36.020
Um, it's, I should have much more simply laid
out in that way during, um, during my appearance

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:42.180
with Rogan, which was to say the real difference
is that Sam is critiquing ideas and not including

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:48.180
identity, whereas Steven Crowder is going
hard on Carlos Mazda's identity and it just

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:52.050
so happens that that is a violation of youtube
terms and conditions.

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:57.610
So I apologize that I did not do as good of
a job as I could have.

00:01:57.610 --> 00:02:02.880
You know, in the heat of the moment, it, you
always come up with better things to say after.

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:08.920
But my understanding was that most of the
conversation was not literally Joe saying

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:14.340
what Crowder did is the same as what Sam did,
but asking me what I thought the differences

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:18.060
were and I don't know that I did the best
job of explaining it at the time.

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:22.260
Uh, although it did lead to this funny moment
where I said, well, if you're saying that

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:29.739
Dave Rubin has a cognitive limitation, then
in a way, maybe Sam is going after him for

00:02:29.739 --> 00:02:31.969
a disability, which of course is not what
I was saying.

00:02:31.969 --> 00:02:35.549
And it's not what I thought Rogan was saying,
but it led to kind of a weird, funny moment.

00:02:35.549 --> 00:02:38.849
A, we'll talk about that again and I think
that that is an issue that's going to come

00:02:38.849 --> 00:02:40.500
up again on the program.

